  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A sample of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.040\\text{ mol}\"></span> of an ideal monatomic gas is contained in a cylinder with a movable piston. The gas undergoes a two-step process, starting from state X, moving to state Y, and finally to state Z. The table below provides the pressure and volume for these states.</p><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Pressure (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P / 10^5\\text{ Pa}\"></span>)</th><th>Volume (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V / 10^{-4}\\text{ m}^3\"></span>)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-label=\"X\"><td>X</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"Y\"><td>Y</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10.0\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"Z\"><td>Z</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P_Z\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"25.0\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Calculate the internal energy of the gas when it is in state X. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> Calculate the work done by the gas during the expansion from state X to state Y. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> The transition from state Y to state Z is an isothermal process. Determine the pressure <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P_Z\"></span> of the gas at state Z. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"d\"><p><strong>d</strong> State and explain the change in internal energy of the gas during the process from Y to Z. [2]</p></section>"
